  "subdivision_of_building": "Rear of existing building",
  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Proposed single storey outbuilding to the rear of the existing building.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The scale, siting and design of the proposed development would result in an increased sense of being&nbsp; overbearing, a harmful loss of outlook and overshadowing to neighbouring occupiers. The outbuilding therefore constitutes unneighbourly development and is contrary to:- National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023)- Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021);- The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012);- Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan: (September 2024)",
    "The application has failed to demonstrate that the outbuilding will remain ancillary to the main dwelling. It would provide all the amenities of a dwellinghouse and benefit from an access route independent of the host dwelling.&nbsp;The proposal therefore represents an&nbsp;inappropriate and uncharacteristic residential form in a rear garden setting&nbsp;which results in harm to the character and context of the area.&nbsp; Insufficient information has also been provided regarding the previously existing access leg to the rear and east of the site. As such, the proposal is contrary to:&nbsp;- National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023)- Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021);- The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012);- Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan: (September 2024)&nbsp;"
  ],
